                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client with iron-deficiency anemia complains of feeling fatigued almost all of the time. The nurse would respond with which statement?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale: \nOxygen is required to meet the metabolic needs of the body. With decreased hemoglobin, such as in iron-deficiency anemia, the oxygen-carrying capacity of the blood is less than normal. The client feels the effects of this change as fatigue. The statements in the remaining options are incorrect.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, iron-deficiency anemia. Think about the pathophysiology associated with iron-deficiency anemia. Recalling that hemoglobin transports most of the oxygen needed for cellular respiration will direct you to the correct option.\n \n\nClient Needs: Physiological Integrity\nClinical Judgment/Cognitive Skill(s): Take Action\nCognitive Ability: Applying\nContent Area: Adult Health: Cardiovascular\nHealth Problem: Adult Health: Hematological: Anemias\nIntegrated Process: Nursing Process/Implementation\nPriority Concepts: Gas Exchange, Perfusion\nStrategies: Subject",
                        "id": "40108c94b7134d0aab1a36b7d1263f10",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "c927870cd2c34584852c161761e42a61",
                                "content": "Avoid driving the car for a few days."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "d0c80632be0d4770aefdd6a36caa9c7b",
                                "content": "Restrict fluid intake to prevent incontinence."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "993434d2c3284ea98a1f65199d808ddb",
                                "content": "Avoid lifting objects heavier than 20 lb (9 kg) for at least 6 weeks."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "3a84a3db08b8442a97bbe8d263c89ea4",
                                "content": "Notify the primary health care provider if small blood clots are noticed during urination."
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
